{"title":"Career Roadmap · Propulsion Engineer","role":"Propulsion Engineer","summary":"A Propulsion Engineer designs, analyses, tests and improves systems that generate thrust for aircraft, spacecraft, missiles, launch vehicles and other aerospace platforms. Depending on specialisation, the engineer may work on gas-turbine engines, rocket engines, electric propulsion, combustion, turbomachinery, propulsion controls, thermal systems or propulsion testing.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, gas dynamics, aerodynamics and propulsion fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Choose aircraft propulsion, rocket propulsion, turbomachinery, combustion, propulsion controls or thermal systems"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress toward propulsion-system development, testing, analysis or technical leadership"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine propulsion with electrification, advanced materials, computational engineering, AI and sustainable propulsion"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Aerospace / Aeronautical Engineering → Propulsion Engineer","text":"Direct alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"Aerospace Engineering provides a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Aerodynamics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Gas dynamics"},{"text":"Aircraft systems"},{"text":"Propulsion"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Control systems"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should additionally develop combustion, turbomachinery, rocket propulsion, CFD, propulsion testing, MATLAB/Simulink, CAD/CAE and experimental methods."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Long-range horizons are planning guidance; exact industry requirements should be verified."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, physics, mechanics, programming and engineering drawing"},{"text":"College coursework + NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Engineering calculations and Python/MATLAB fundamentals"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, materials and electrical fundamentals"},{"text":"Aerospace coursework + NPTEL"},{"text":"Thermal/fluid laboratory experiments"},{"text":"Thermal foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Aerodynamics, compressible flow, gas dynamics and heat transfer"},{"text":"Aerospace labs"},{"text":"Analyse nozzle and aerodynamic-flow problems"},{"text":"Fluid/thermal capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Aircraft propulsion, turbomachinery, combustion and engine cycles"},{"text":"Propulsion laboratory"},{"text":"Analyse Brayton-cycle and engine performance"},{"text":"Propulsion foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Turbines, compressors, combustors, nozzles and propulsion components"},{"text":"Propulsion projects + CAE"},{"text":"Design/analyse a propulsion component"},{"text":"Propulsion engineering"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Rocket propulsion, propulsion controls, CFD and experimental testing"},{"text":"Research/industry internship"},{"text":"Simulate or test a propulsion system"},{"text":"Advanced propulsion"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced CFD, combustion modelling, engine performance, instrumentation and test planning"},{"text":"Industry/research project"},{"text":"Complete a propulsion-analysis project"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Full propulsion capstone, testing, optimisation, technical documentation and interview preparation"},{"text":"Industry mentor + capstone"},{"text":"End-to-end propulsion project"},{"text":"Job readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Technical Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Thermofluids"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Compressible flow"},{"text":"Gas dynamics"},{"text":"Boundary layers"},{"text":"Nozzle flow"},{"text":"Shock waves"},{"text":"Combustion fundamentals"},{"text":"Heat exchangers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aircraft Propulsion"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Turbojet"},{"text":"Turbofan"},{"text":"Turboprop"},{"text":"Turboshaft"},{"text":"Ramjet"},{"text":"Scramjet"},{"text":"Gas-turbine cycles"},{"text":"Compressor stages"},{"text":"Turbine stages"},{"text":"Combustion chambers"},{"text":"Exhaust nozzles"},{"text":"Afterburners"},{"text":"Engine performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rocket Propulsion"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Solid rocket motors"},{"text":"Liquid rocket engines"},{"text":"Hybrid rocket engines"},{"text":"Cryogenic propulsion"},{"text":"Propellant fundamentals"},{"text":"Combustion chambers"},{"text":"Injectors"},{"text":"Nozzles"},{"text":"Thrust"},{"text":"Specific impulse"},{"text":"Characteristic velocity"},{"text":"Thrust-to-weight ratio"},{"text":"Staging concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Propulsion Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thrust measurement"},{"text":"Pressure measurement"},{"text":"Temperature measurement"},{"text":"Flow measurement"},{"text":"Engine instrumentation"},{"text":"Data acquisition"},{"text":"Test-cell operations"},{"text":"Vibration measurement"},{"text":"Engine performance testing"},{"text":"Test safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software & CAE Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise:"},{"type":"